<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Learn 2D and 3D frame finite element analysis, from element stiffness to support reactions."><title>FrameLab Â· FEM Learning Studio</title><style>:root{--ink:#182f35;--muted:#65787b;--teal:#087f77;--paper:#f4f6f3;--line:#dce3dd;--orange:#ba663d}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);font:14px/1.55 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',sans-serif;color:var(--ink)}button,input,select{font:inherit}button,.button{cursor:pointer;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;background:white;padding:8px 12px;color:var(--ink);display:inline-block}button:hover,.button:hover{border-color:var(--teal);background:#eef6f1}button:focus-visible,input:focus-visible,select:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--teal);outline-offset:3px}button:disabled{opacity:.4;cursor:default}header{height:78px;background:#fff;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:0 4vw}.brand{font-weight:700;font-size:23px;text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:center}.mark{background:var(--ink);color:#fff;width:36px;height:36px;border-radius:8px;text-align:center}.mark span{color:#86d9c0}.tag{font-size:9px;letter-spacing:2px;color:var(--muted);margin-left:12px;font-weight:500}main{max-width:1600px;padding:34px 4vw 0;margin:auto}.intro{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;margin-bottom:32px}.eyebrow,.section-caption{font-size:10px;letter-spacing:1.8px;font-weight:700;color:var(--muted)}h1{font:42px/1.12 Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-1px;margin:15px 0}h1 em{color:var(--teal);font-weight:400}.intro p{color:var(--muted);margin:0}.intro-note{padding:24px 0 24px 30px;border-left:1px solid var(--line);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:1px}.intro-note strong{display:block;font-size:18px;letter-spacing:0;margin:12px 0 3px}.intro-note small{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);letter-spacing:0}.live-dot{display:inline-block;width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--teal);margin-right:5px}.workspace{display:grid;grid-template-columns:350px minmax(0,1fr);gap:22px;align-items:start}aside,.main-pane{background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden}aside{padding:22px}.field{display:block;margin:20px 0;color:var(--muted);font-size:12px}select{width:100%;margin-top:6px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:5px;background:white;padding:10px;color:var(--ink)}h2{font-size:17px;margin:4px 0}.line{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:8px;align-items:center}.pill{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;font-size:10px;white-space:nowrap}.unit-row{display:flex;gap:12px;margin-top:15px}.unit-row label{width:50%;font-size:11px;color:var(--muted)}input{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:4px;padding:5px;min-width:0;color:var(--ink);background:white}.unit-row input{display:block;width:100%}.hint{font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.5}.edit-tabs{display:flex;margin:20px -5px 12px;gap:3px}.edit-tabs button{border:0;padding:7px;font-size:11px}.active{color:var(--teal)!important;background:#e8f3ed!important}.node-card{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:7px;padding:10px;margin:10px 0}.node-card h3{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:12px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center}.delete{padding:1px 7px;color:var(--muted);font-size:12px}.grid-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:7px}.grid-fields label{font-size:10px;color:var(--muted)}.grid-fields input,.grid-fields select{width:100%;padding:5px;margin:2px 0}.bc{margin-top:10px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:8px}.bc-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:28px 48px 1fr;align-items:center;gap:5px;font-size:10px;margin:5px 0}.bc-row input[type=number]{width:100%}.presets{display:flex;gap:4px;margin-bottom:6px}.presets button{padding:3px 6px;font-size:10px}.wide{width:100%}.primary{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;width:100%;background:var(--teal);color:white;border-color:var(--teal);margin:15px 0;padding:12px 15px;font-weight:600}.primary:hover{background:#066b64;color:#fff}details{font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:10px}summary{cursor:pointer;color:var(--ink)}#error{color:#a33e26;background:#fff1eb;border-radius:5px;font-size:12px}#error:not(:empty){padding:10px;margin-top:10px}.viewer-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;padding:22px 24px 10px}.viewer-controls{display:flex;gap:16px;padding:4px 24px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:11px;color:var(--muted)}.viewer-controls label{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:5px}.viewer-controls input[type=number]{width:62px}.viewer-controls input[type=range]{width:75px}.drawing{height:345px;background-color:#fafcf9;background-image:radial-gradient(#cfd9d1 .7px,transparent .7px);background-size:18px 18px;margin:12px 18px 0;border:1px solid #e4e9e3;border-radius:8px}.drawing svg{width:100%;height:100%}.legend{display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;padding:12px;font-size:10px;color:var(--muted)}.legend i{display:inline-block;width:16px;height:2px;vertical-align:middle;background:var(--ink);margin-right:5px}.legend i.teal{background:var(--teal)}.legend i.orange{background:var(--orange)}.metrics{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:4px}.metric{padding:16px 24px;border-right:1px solid var(--line)}.metric:last-child{border:0}.metric small{display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:1px}.metric strong{font-size:22px;font-weight:500}.metric span{font-size:11px;color:var(--muted)}.walkthrough{padding:24px}nav{display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:15px 0 24px}nav button{font-size:11px;padding:6px 9px}#lesson h2{font:26px Georgia,serif;margin-bottom:10px}#lesson p{color:var(--muted);font-size:13px;max-width:850px}.equation{background:#edf4ee;border-left:3px solid var(--teal);padding:14px 18px;margin:16px 0;font:17px/1.8 Georgia,serif;overflow:auto}.matrix-wrap{overflow:auto;max-height:420px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;margin:12px 0}.matrix{border-collapse:collapse;white-space:nowrap;font:11px/1.5 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Consolas,monospace;width:100%;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.matrix td,.matrix th{padding:7px 10px;text-align:right;border-bottom:1px solid #edf0ec}.matrix th{background:#f2f5ef;color:var(--muted);font-weight:500;position:sticky;top:0;z-index:1}.matrix th:first-child{left:0;z-index:2}.matrix td:first-child{background:#f6f8f4;position:sticky;left:0}.matrix .nz{color:var(--teal);background:#edf7f0}.matrix .selected{background:#d7eee0}.lesson-bottom{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;margin-top:24px;font-size:11px;color:var(--muted)}.select-row{display:flex;gap:15px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:14px 0}.select-row select{width:auto;margin:0;max-width:100%}.note{padding:12px 15px;border:1px solid #dce8df;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}footer{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:26px 0;color:var(--muted);font-size:11px}footer button{border:0;background:none;padding:0 4px;font-size:11px;text-decoration:underline}dialog{max-width:750px;width:90vw;max-height:85vh;overflow:auto;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:32px;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.7}dialog::backdrop{background:#102b3355}.close{float:right;font-size:20px;padding:0 9px}dialog h2{font:28px Georgia,serif}code{font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:11px}a{color:var(--teal)}.subhead{font-size:13px;margin-top:20px}.member-hit{cursor:pointer}.member-hit:hover{stroke:#b3dcd1}.muted{color:var(--muted)}@media(min-width:1500px){.drawing{height:410px}}@media(max-width:1000px){.workspace{grid-template-columns:300px minmax(0,1fr)}main{padding:25px 2vw 0}.walkthrough{padding:18px}.intro-note{display:none}.metric{padding:12px}.tag{display:none}}@media(max-width:760px){header{height:auto;padding:16px;gap:15px;flex-wrap:wrap}header button,.button{font-size:12px}.workspace{display:flex;flex-direction:column}aside,.main-pane{width:100%}.intro{padding:0 10px}h1{font-size:34px}.intro p{font-size:12px}.drawing{height:310px}.legend{gap:10px}.metrics{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}.metric strong{font-size:17px}footer{display:block}.edit-tabs button{font-size:12px}.grid-fields{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}}@media print{header,aside,.intro,.viewer-controls,nav,.lesson-bottom,footer{display:none}.workspace{display:block}.main-pane{border:0}.matrix-wrap{max-height:none;overflow:visible}body{background:white}}
</style></head><body>
<header><a class="brand" href="#"><span class="mark">F<span>âŒ</span></span> FrameLab<span class="tag">LEARNING STUDIO</span></a><div><button id="guide">User guide</button> <button id="export">â†“ Save model</button> <label class="button">â†‘ Open model<input id="import" type="file" accept="application/json,.json" hidden></label></div></header>
<main><div class="intro"><div><div class="eyebrow">STRUCTURAL MECHANICS / FINITE ELEMENT METHOD</div><h1>See the structure.<br><em>Understand the solution.</em></h1><p>A transparent journey from individual members to the complete system.</p></div><div class="intro-note"><span class="live-dot"></span> DETERMINISTIC Â· RUNS OFFLINE<br><strong>2D + 3D frame analysis</strong><small>Axial Â· Bending Â· Torsion</small></div></div>
<div class="workspace"><aside><div class="section-caption">01 / DEFINE YOUR MODEL</div><label class="field">Start with an example<select id="example"><option value="portal">2D Â· Textbook portal frame</option><option value="spatial">3D Â· Combined-load cantilever</option><option value="spaceFrame">3D Â· Bent frame</option></select></label><div class="line"><h2 id="model-title"></h2><span id="dimension" class="pill"></span></div><div class="unit-row"><label>Length unit<input id="length-unit" aria-label="Length unit"></label><label>Force unit<input id="force-unit" aria-label="Force unit"></label></div><p class="hint">Use one consistent unit system. Changing these labels does not convert values.</p><div class="edit-tabs"><button data-edit="nodes" class="active">Nodes & supports</button><button data-edit="elements">Members</button><button data-edit="loads">Loads</button></div><div id="editor"></div><div id="error" role="alert"></div><button id="solve" class="primary">Solve & explore <span>â†—</span></button><p class="hint">Linear elastic Eulerâ€“Bernoulli members. Small displacements, rigid joints, nodal loads.</p><details><summary>Model assumptions & scope</summary><p>Prismatic members; axial extension, bending without shear deformation, and Saint-Venant torsion in 3D. No geometric nonlinearity, internal releases, distributed member loads, or tapered sections. Rotations are radians; member roll is degrees. An internal hinge differs from a pinned support and is not modeled here.</p></details></aside>
<section class="main-pane"><div class="viewer-head"><div><div class="section-caption">MODEL VIEW</div><h2 id="view-title">Textbook portal frame</h2></div><span id="status" class="pill">Ready</span></div><div class="viewer-controls"><label><input id="show-deformed" type="checkbox" checked> Deformed shape</label><label>Scale <input id="scale" type="number" min="0" step="1" value="100"></label><label id="azimuth-wrap">Orbit <input id="azimuth" type="range" min="0" max="360" value="35"></label><label id="elevation-wrap">Elevation <input id="elevation" type="range" min="-80" max="80" value="25"></label></div><div id="drawing" class="drawing"></div><div class="legend"><span><i></i> Original</span><span><i class="teal"></i> Deformed</span><span><i class="orange"></i> Applied load</span><span>Click a member to inspect it</span></div><div id="metrics" class="metrics"></div>
<div class="walkthrough"><div class="section-caption">02 / FOLLOW THE MATHEMATICS</div><nav id="stages" aria-label="Solution stages"></nav><div id="lesson"></div><div class="lesson-bottom"><button id="prev">â† Previous</button><span id="stage-count"></span><button id="next">Next step â†’</button></div></div></section></div><footer>FrameLab / Bonus Assignment #2 <span>Implemented mathematics. No AI calls at runtime. <button id="disclosure">AI disclosure</button></span></footer></main>
<dialog id="modal"><button id="close-modal" class="close" aria-label="Close">Ã—</button><div id="modal-body"></div></dialog>
<script>/* FrameLab: deterministic linear elastic Eulerâ€“Bernoulli frame FEM. */
(function(root){
'use strict';
const zeros=(r,c)=>Array.from({length:r},()=>Array(c).fill(0));
const transpose=a=>a[0].map((_,i)=>a.map(r=>r[i]));
const mul=(a,b)=>a.map(r=>b[0].map((_,j)=>r.reduce((s,v,k)=>s+v*b[k][j],0)));
const mv=(a,v)=>a.map(r=>r.reduce((s,x,i)=>s+x*v[i],0));
const dot=(a,b)=>a.reduce((s,v,i)=>s+v*b[i],0);
const cross=(a,b)=>[a[1]*b[2]-a[2]*b[1],a[2]*b[0]-a[0]*b[2],a[0]*b[1]-a[1]*b[0]];
const norm=a=>Math.hypot(...a), unit=a=>a.map(x=>x/norm(a));
const labels=d=>d===2?['ux','uy','rz']:['ux','uy','uz','rx','ry','rz'];
function element(model,e){
 const d=model.dimension,p=d===2?3:6, a=model.nodes.find(n=>n.id===e.a),b=model.nodes.find(n=>n.id===e.b);
 if(!a||!b)throw Error(`Element ${e.id}: endpoint node does not exist.`);
 const delta=[b.x-a.x,b.y-a.y,d===3?b.z-a.z:0],L=norm(delta);
 if(!(L>0))throw Error(`Element ${e.id}: length must be positive.`);
 for(const key of d===2?['E','A','Iz']:['E','G','A','Iy','Iz','J'])if(!Number.isFinite(e[key])||e[key]<=0)throw Error(`Element ${e.id}: ${key} must be positive.`);
 const k=zeros(2*p,2*p),parts={axial:zeros(2*p,2*p),bendingZ:zeros(2*p,2*p)};
 function block(part,indices,values){indices.forEach((i,r)=>indices.forEach((j,c)=>{k[i][j]+=values[r][c];part[i][j]+=values[r][c];}));}
 const EA=e.E*e.A/L;
 block(parts.axial,[0,p],[[EA,-EA],[-EA,EA]]);
 const bending=(EI,sign)=>{const a=12*EI/L**3,b=sign*6*EI/L**2,c=4*EI/L,f=2*EI/L;return [[a,b,-a,b],[b,c,-b,f],[-a,-b,a,-b],[b,f,-b,c]];};
 block(parts.bendingZ,d===2?[1,2,4,5]:[1,5,7,11],bending(e.E*e.Iz,1));
 let R,T=zeros(2*p,2*p);
 if(d===2){const c=delta[0]/L,s=delta[1]/L;R=[[c,s,0],[-s,c,0],[0,0,1]];for(let h=0;h<2;h++)for(let i=0;i<3;i++)for(let j=0;j<3;j++)T[3*h+i][3*h+j]=R[i][j];}
 else {
  parts.bendingY=zeros(12,12);parts.torsion=zeros(12,12);
  block(parts.bendingY,[2,4,8,10],bending(e.E*e.Iy,-1));
  const GJ=e.G*e.J/L;block(parts.torsion,[3,9],[[GJ,-GJ],[-GJ,GJ]]);
  const x=unit(delta),ref=Math.abs(x[2])<0.9?[0,0,1]:[0,1,0],y0=unit(cross(ref,x)),z0=cross(x,y0),r=(e.roll||0)*Math.PI/180;
  const y=y0.map((v,i)=>v*Math.cos(r)+z0[i]*Math.sin(r)),z=z0.map((v,i)=>v*Math.cos(r)-y0[i]*Math.sin(r));R=[x,y,z];
  for(let h=0;h<4;h++)for(let i=0;i<3;i++)for(let j=0;j<3;j++)T[3*h+i][3*h+j]=R[i][j];
 }
 const ia=model.nodes.indexOf(a),ib=model.nodes.indexOf(b),map=[...Array(p).keys()].map(i=>ia*p+i).concat([...Array(p).keys()].map(i=>ib*p+i));
 return {e,L,k,parts,R,T,kg:mul(transpose(T),mul(k,T)),map,a,b};
}
function validate(m){
 if(![2,3].includes(m.dimension))throw Error('Dimension must be 2 or 3.');
 if(!Array.isArray(m.nodes)||!m.nodes.length||!Array.isArray(m.elements)||!m.elements.length)throw Error('Add at least two nodes and one element.');
 for(const key of ['nodes','elements']){const ids=m[key].map(x=>x.id);if(ids.some(x=>!Number.isInteger(x)||x<1)||new Set(ids).size!==ids.length)throw Error(`${key}: IDs must be unique positive integers.`);}
 const p=labels(m.dimension).length;
 for(const n of m.nodes){for(const key of m.dimension===2?['x','y']:['x','y','z'])if(!Number.isFinite(n[key]))throw Error(`Node ${n.id}: invalid ${key}.`);
 if(!Array.isArray(n.loads)||n.loads.length!==p||n.loads.some(x=>!Number.isFinite(x)))throw Error(`Node ${n.id}: provide ${p} finite loads.`);
 if(!Array.isArray(n.prescribed)||n.prescribed.length!==p||n.prescribed.some(x=>x!==null&&!Number.isFinite(x)))throw Error(`Node ${n.id}: restraints must be null (free) or a finite prescribed value.`);}
 for(const e of m.elements)if(e.roll!==undefined&&!Number.isFinite(e.roll))throw Error(`Element ${e.id}: roll must be finite.`);
}
function solve(m){
 validate(m);const p=labels(m.dimension).length,N=p*m.nodes.length,K=zeros(N,N),F=m.nodes.flatMap(n=>n.loads),u=Array(N).fill(0),free=[],fixed=[];
 const elements=m.elements.map(e=>element(m,e));
 for(const el of elements)el.map.forEach((i,r)=>el.map.forEach((j,c)=>K[i][j]+=el.kg[r][c]));
 m.nodes.forEach((n,i)=>n.prescribed.forEach((v,j)=>{if(v===null)free.push(i*p+j);else {fixed.push(i*p+j);u[i*p+j]=v;}}));
 const A=free.map(i=>free.map(j=>K[i][j])),rhs=free.map(i=>F[i]-fixed.reduce((s,j)=>s+K[i][j]*u[j],0));
 // Symmetric diagonal scaling controls translation/rotation unit disparity.
 const scales=A.map((r,i)=>{if(!(r[i]>0))throw Error(`Unstable structure: ${dofName(m,free[i])} has no stiffness.`);return Math.sqrt(r[i]);});
 const B=A.map((r,i)=>r.map((v,j)=>v/scales[i]/scales[j])),b=rhs.map((v,i)=>v/scales[i]),U=B.map(r=>r.slice()),g=b.slice(),steps=[];
 for(let k=0;k<free.length;k++){
  let pivot=k;for(let i=k+1;i<free.length;i++)if(Math.abs(U[i][k])>Math.abs(U[pivot][k]))pivot=i;
  if(Math.abs(U[pivot][k])<1e-12)throw Error('Unstable or numerically singular structure: add appropriate supports or check member connectivity and stiffness ratios.');
  if(pivot!==k){[U[k],U[pivot]]=[U[pivot],U[k]];[g[k],g[pivot]]=[g[pivot],g[k]];}
  const factors=[];for(let i=k+1;i<free.length;i++){const factor=U[i][k]/U[k][k];if(factor!==0)factors.push({row:i,factor});U[i][k]=0;for(let j=k+1;j<free.length;j++)U[i][j]-=factor*U[k][j];g[i]-=factor*g[k];}
  steps.push({column:k,pivotRow:pivot,pivot:U[k][k],factors});
 }
 const y=Array(free.length).fill(0),back=[];
 for(let i=free.length-1;i>=0;i--){const sum=U[i].reduce((s,v,j)=>j>i?s+v*y[j]:s,0);y[i]=(g[i]-sum)/U[i][i];back.push({row:i,rhs:g[i],sum,pivot:U[i][i],y:y[i]});}
 free.forEach((v,i)=>u[v]=y[i]/scales[i]);const Ku=mv(K,u),reactions=Ku.map((v,i)=>v-F[i]);
 if(u.some(v=>!Number.isFinite(v)))throw Error('Numerical overflow: check units and material properties.');
 elements.forEach(el=>{el.globalU=el.map.map(i=>u[i]);el.localU=mv(el.T,el.globalU);el.forces=mv(el.k,el.localU);});
 const residual=free.reduce((s,i)=>Math.max(s,Math.abs(reactions[i])),0),relativeResidual=residual/Math.max(1,...F.map(Math.abs),...Ku.map(Math.abs));
 return {K,F,u,free,fixed,A,rhs,scales,B,b,U,g,y,steps,back,reactions,elements,residual,relativeResidual};
}
function dofName(m,i){const p=labels(m.dimension).length;return `N${m.nodes[Math.floor(i/p)].id}.${labels(m.dimension)[i%p]}`;}
function curve(el,dimension,t){const v=el.localU,p=dimension===2?3:6,L=el.L,N1=1-3*t*t+2*t*t*t,N2=L*(t-2*t*t+t*t*t),N3=3*t*t-2*t*t*t,N4=L*(-t*t+t*t*t);let local;
 if(dimension===2)local=[v[0]*(1-t)+v[3]*t,N1*v[1]+N2*v[2]+N3*v[4]+N4*v[5],0];
 else local=[v[0]*(1-t)+v[6]*t,N1*v[1]+N2*v[5]+N3*v[7]+N4*v[11],N1*v[2]-N2*v[4]+N3*v[8]-N4*v[10]];
 return mv(transpose(el.R),local);
}
function node(id,x,y,z,p,loads,fix){return {id,x,y,z,loads:loads||Array(p).fill(0),prescribed:fix||Array(p).fill(null)};}
const examples={
 portal:()=>({name:'Textbook portal frame',dimension:2,lengthUnit:'in',forceUnit:'lb',nodes:[node(1,-60,0,0,3,null,[0,0,0]),node(2,-60,120,0,3,[10000,0,0]),node(3,60,120,0,3,[0,0,5000]),node(4,60,0,0,3,null,[0,0,0])],elements:[{id:1,a:1,b:2,E:30e6,A:10,Iz:200},{id:2,a:2,b:3,E:30e6,A:10,Iz:100},{id:3,a:3,b:4,E:30e6,A:10,Iz:200}]}),
 spatial:()=>({name:'3D cantilever â€¢ combined loading',dimension:3,lengthUnit:'m',forceUnit:'N',nodes:[node(1,0,0,0,6,null,[0,0,0,0,0,0]),node(2,3,0,0,6,[10000,-1000,-1500,600,0,0])],elements:[{id:1,a:1,b:2,E:210e9,G:80e9,A:0.01,Iy:8e-6,Iz:6e-6,J:1e-5,roll:0}]}),
 spaceFrame:()=>({name:'3D bent frame',dimension:3,lengthUnit:'m',forceUnit:'N',nodes:[node(1,0,0,0,6,null,[0,0,0,0,0,0]),node(2,0,0,3,6),node(3,3,0,3,6),node(4,3,2,3,6,[500,-800,-1200,200,0,0])],elements:[[1,2],[2,3],[3,4]].map(([a,b],i)=>({id:i+1,a,b,E:210e9,G:80e9,A:0.01,Iy:8e-6,Iz:6e-6,J:1e-5,roll:0}))})
};
const api={zeros,transpose,mul,mv,labels,element,solve,dofName,curve,examples};if(typeof module!=='undefined')module.exports=api;else root.FEM=api;
})(typeof window!=='undefined'?window:globalThis);
</script><script>'use strict';
const $=id=>document.getElementById(id),esc=s=>String(s).replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));
const fmt=x=>!Number.isFinite(x)?'â€”':Math.abs(x)<1e-13?'0':Math.abs(x)>=1e5||Math.abs(x)<1e-3?x.toExponential(5):Number(x.toPrecision(7)).toString();
let model=FEM.examples.portal(),result=null,stage=0,edit='nodes',selected=0,part='combined',matrixRow=0,matrixCol=0,elim=0,dirty=false;
const stages=['Model & DOFs','Element stiffness','Transform','Assembly','Constraints','Solve','Results'];
const p=()=>FEM.labels(model.dimension).length, names=()=>model.nodes.flatMap((n,i)=>FEM.labels(model.dimension).map((_,j)=>FEM.dofName(model,i*p()+j)));
function table(A,rows,cols,highlight=false){return `<div class="matrix-wrap"><table class="matrix"><thead><tr><th>DOF</th>${cols.map(c=>`<th>${esc(c)}</th>`).join('')}</tr></thead><tbody>${A.map((r,i)=>`<tr><td>${esc(rows[i])}</td>${r.map(v=>`<td class="${highlight&&v!==0?'nz':''}">${fmt(v)}</td>`).join('')}</tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div>`;}
function eq(s){return `<div class="equation">${s}</div>`;}
function selectEl(){return `<div class="select-row"><label>Inspect member <select id="element-select">${model.elements.map((e,i)=>`<option value="${i}" ${i===selected?'selected':''}>E${e.id} Â· N${e.a} â†’ N${e.b}</option>`).join('')}</select></label></div>`;}
function syncTitle(){ $('model-title').textContent=model.name;$('view-title').textContent=model.name;$('dimension').textContent=model.dimension+'D';$('length-unit').value=model.lengthUnit;$('force-unit').value=model.forceUnit;['azimuth-wrap','elevation-wrap'].forEach(id=>$(id).style.display=model.dimension===3?'flex':'none');}
function field(label,value,attrs){return `<label>${label}<input type="number" step="any" value="${value}" ${attrs}></label>`;}
function renderEditor(){syncTitle();document.querySelectorAll('[data-edit]').forEach(b=>b.classList.toggle('active',b.dataset.edit===edit));const labs=FEM.labels(model.dimension),d=p();
 if(edit==='nodes')$('editor').innerHTML=model.nodes.map((n,i)=>`<div class="node-card"><h3>NODE ${n.id}<button class="delete" data-delete-node="${i}" aria-label="Remove node ${n.id}">Ã—</button></h3><div class="grid-fields">${(model.dimension===2?['x','y']:['x','y','z']).map(k=>field(k,n[k],`data-node="${i}" data-key="${k}" aria-label="Node ${n.id} ${k}"`)).join('')}</div><div class="bc"><div class="presets"><button data-preset="fixed" data-node="${i}">Fixed</button><button data-preset="pin" data-node="${i}">Pinned</button><button data-preset="free" data-node="${i}">Free</button></div>${labs.map((k,j)=>`<div class="bc-row"><label for="bc-${i}-${j}">${k}</label><label><input id="bc-${i}-${j}" type="checkbox" data-bc="${i}" data-dof="${j}" ${n.prescribed[j]!==null?'checked':''}> set</label><input type="number" step="any" data-value="${i}" data-dof="${j}" value="${n.prescribed[j]??0}" ${n.prescribed[j]===null?'disabled':''} aria-label="Node ${n.id} prescribed ${k}"></div>`).join('')}</div></div>`).join('')+'<button class="wide" id="add-node">+ Add node</button><p class="hint">Checked = prescribed movement; unchecked = free. Translations use the length unit; rotations use radians.</p>';
 else if(edit==='loads')$('editor').innerHTML='<p class="hint">Global axes; positive moments follow the right-hand rule. Forces use '+esc(model.forceUnit)+'; moments use '+esc(model.forceUnit)+'Â·'+esc(model.lengthUnit)+'.</p>'+model.nodes.map((n,i)=>`<div class="node-card"><h3>NODE ${n.id}</h3><div class="grid-fields">${labs.map((k,j)=>field((j<(model.dimension===2?2:3)?'F':'M')+k.slice(1),n.loads[j],`data-load="${i}" data-dof="${j}" aria-label="Node ${n.id} load ${k}"`)).join('')}</div></div>`).join('');
 else $('editor').innerHTML='<p class="hint">E, G: force/lengthÂ²; A: lengthÂ²; I, J: lengthâ´. Roll rotates the 3D section axes about local x.</p>'+model.elements.map((e,i)=>`<div class="node-card"><h3>MEMBER ${e.id}<button class="delete" data-delete-element="${i}" aria-label="Remove member ${e.id}">Ã—</button></h3><div class="grid-fields">${['a','b'].map(k=>`<label>${k==='a'?'From node':'To node'}<select data-element="${i}" data-key="${k}">${model.nodes.map(n=>`<option value="${n.id}" ${n.id===e[k]?'selected':''}>${n.id}</option>`).join('')}</select></label>`).join('')}${(model.dimension===2?['E','A','Iz']:['E','G','A','Iy','Iz','J','roll']).map(k=>field(k,e[k]||0,`data-element="${i}" data-key="${k}" aria-label="Member ${e.id} ${k}"`)).join('')}</div></div>`).join('')+'<button class="wide" id="add-element">+ Add member</button>';
}
function markDirty(){dirty=true;result=null;$('status').textContent='Model changed Â· solve again';$('status').style.color='';$('error').textContent='';draw();renderLesson();$('metrics').innerHTML='<div class="metric"><small>MODEL UPDATED</small><span>Solve to refresh calculations.</span></div>';}
$('editor').addEventListener('change',ev=>{const t=ev.target,x=t.dataset,v=Number(t.value);if(x.node!==undefined&&x.key)model.nodes[+x.node][x.key]=v;else if(x.element!==undefined)model.elements[+x.element][x.key]=v;else if(x.load!==undefined)model.nodes[+x.load].loads[+x.dof]=v;else if(x.bc!==undefined){model.nodes[+x.bc].prescribed[+x.dof]=t.checked?0:null;renderEditor();}else if(x.value!==undefined)model.nodes[+x.value].prescribed[+x.dof]=v;markDirty();});
$('editor').addEventListener('click',ev=>{const t=ev.target,x=t.dataset;if(x.preset){const n=model.nodes[+x.node];n.prescribed=Array(p()).fill(null);if(x.preset==='fixed')n.prescribed.fill(0);if(x.preset==='pin')for(let j=0;j<(model.dimension===2?2:3);j++)n.prescribed[j]=0;}
 else if(x.deleteNode!==undefined){const id=model.nodes[+x.deleteNode].id;model.nodes.splice(+x.deleteNode,1);model.elements=model.elements.filter(e=>e.a!==id&&e.b!==id);selected=0;}
 else if(x.deleteElement!==undefined){model.elements.splice(+x.deleteElement,1);selected=0;}
 else if(t.id==='add-node'){const id=Math.max(0,...model.nodes.map(n=>n.id))+1,last=model.nodes.at(-1);model.nodes.push({id,x:(last?.x||0)+1,y:last?.y||0,z:last?.z||0,loads:Array(p()).fill(0),prescribed:Array(p()).fill(null)});}
 else if(t.id==='add-element'){if(model.nodes.length<2){$('error').textContent='Add at least two nodes first.';return;}const e=model.elements[0]||{E:210e9,G:80e9,A:0.01,Iy:8e-6,Iz:6e-6,J:1e-5,roll:0};model.elements.push({...e,id:Math.max(0,...model.elements.map(e=>e.id))+1,a:model.nodes[0].id,b:model.nodes.at(-1).id});}
 else return;renderEditor();markDirty();});
// Separate variable declaration avoids implicit globals in event callbacks.
function solve(){try{result=FEM.solve(model);dirty=false;$('error').textContent='';$('status').textContent='Equilibrium verified';$('status').style.color='var(--teal)';selected=Math.min(selected,model.elements.length-1);elim=0;matrixRow=matrixCol=0;const maxU=Math.max(...model.nodes.map((_,i)=>Math.hypot(...result.u.slice(i*p(),i*p()+(model.dimension===2?2:3)))));$('metrics').innerHTML=`<div class="metric"><small>MODEL SIZE</small><strong>${model.nodes.length} / ${model.elements.length}</strong> <span>nodes / members</span></div><div class="metric"><small>FREE DOFs</small><strong>${result.free.length}</strong> <span>of ${result.u.length}</span></div><div class="metric"><small>MAX TRANSLATION</small><strong>${fmt(maxU)}</strong> <span>${esc(model.lengthUnit)}</span></div>`;renderLesson();draw();}catch(e){result=null;$('error').textContent=e.message;$('status').textContent='Check model';$('status').style.color='#a33e26';$('metrics').innerHTML='';renderLesson();draw();}}
function renderLesson(){ $('stages').innerHTML=stages.map((s,i)=>`<button data-stage="${i}" class="${i===stage?'active':''}">${i+1}. ${s}</button>`).join('');$('prev').disabled=stage===0;$('next').disabled=stage===stages.length-1;$('stage-count').textContent=`${stage+1} / ${stages.length}`;
 if(!result){$('lesson').innerHTML=`<h2>${dirty?'Ready for a new solution':'Check your structure'}</h2><p>${dirty?'Select Solve & explore to update every matrix, calculation, and result for the edited model.':'Correct the model input and solve again. Disconnected nodes and insufficient restraints can make the system singular.'}</p>`;return;}
 const r=result,el=r.elements[selected],n=names(),local=model.dimension===2?['ui','vi','Î¸zi','uj','vj','Î¸zj']:['ui','vi','wi','Î¸xi','Î¸yi','Î¸zi','uj','vj','wj','Î¸xj','Î¸yj','Î¸zj'];let html='';
 if(stage===0){html=`<h2>A structure becomes a set of unknowns.</h2><p>Each node has ${p()} degrees of freedom (DOFs). A DOF is one independent translation or rotation. Members share the DOFs of their connecting nodes, which enforces displacement compatibility at rigid joints.</p>${eq(`N<sub>DOF</sub> = ${model.nodes.length} nodes Ã— ${p()} DOFs/node = ${r.u.length}`)}<p>Global order is node array order, then ${FEM.labels(model.dimension).join(', ')}. Positive rotations follow the right-hand rule. Translation units are ${esc(model.lengthUnit)}; rotations are radians.</p>${table(model.nodes.map((nd,i)=>[...Array(p()).keys()].map(j=>i*p()+j+1)),model.nodes.map(x=>'N'+x.id),FEM.labels(model.dimension))}<div class="note">${model.dimension===2?'In 2D, ux and uy describe axial and transverse movement in global axes; rz describes in-plane bending rotation.':'In 3D, ux, uy, uz are translations; rx, ry, rz are rotations. A memberâ€™s axial, bending, and torsional responses are defined in its own local axes.'} Fixed supports prescribe every DOF; pinned supports prescribe translations and leave rotations free.</div>`;}
 if(stage===1){const blocks=el.parts,active=part==='combined'?el.k:blocks[part]||el.k;html=`<h2>Build one member from physical responses.</h2>${selectEl()}<p>Member E${el.e.id} has length L = ${fmt(el.L)} ${esc(model.lengthUnit)}. The local x-axis points from N${el.e.a} to N${el.e.b}. Superpose the independent axial, bending${model.dimension===3?', and torsional':''} contributions.</p>${eq('k<sub>local</sub> = k<sub>axial</sub> + k<sub>bending z</sub>'+(model.dimension===3?' + k<sub>bending y</sub> + k<sub>torsion</sub>':''))}<p>For axial extension, strain Îµ = (uâ±¼ âˆ’ uáµ¢)/L and force N = EAÎµ. This gives the [1, âˆ’1; âˆ’1, 1] block multiplied by EA/L = ${fmt(el.e.E*el.e.A/el.L)}.</p><p>For bending, approximate v(x) with cubic Hermite shape functions so the endpoint displacements and slopes match nodal values. Strain energy is Â½âˆ«EI(vâ€³)Â² dx; differentiating twice with respect to nodal DOFs gives the bending stiffness block.</p>${eq('t = x/L; &nbsp; Nâ‚ = 1 âˆ’ 3tÂ² + 2tÂ³; &nbsp; Nâ‚‚ = L(t âˆ’ 2tÂ² + tÂ³)<br>Nâ‚ƒ = 3tÂ² âˆ’ 2tÂ³; &nbsp; Nâ‚„ = L(âˆ’tÂ² + tÂ³)<br>v(x) = Nâ‚váµ¢ + Nâ‚‚Î¸záµ¢ + Nâ‚ƒvâ±¼ + Nâ‚„Î¸zâ±¼')}<p>The bending-z block acts on [váµ¢, Î¸záµ¢, vâ±¼, Î¸zâ±¼]. Its coefficients are a = 12EI/LÂ³, b = 6EI/LÂ², c = 4EI/L, d = 2EI/L.</p><div class="note">For this member, EIz = ${fmt(el.e.E*el.e.Iz)}; a = ${fmt(12*el.e.E*el.e.Iz/el.L**3)}, b = ${fmt(6*el.e.E*el.e.Iz/el.L**2)}, c = ${fmt(4*el.e.E*el.e.Iz/el.L)}, d = ${fmt(2*el.e.E*el.e.Iz/el.L)}.${model.dimension===3?' EIy = '+fmt(el.e.E*el.e.Iy)+'; GJ/L = '+fmt(el.e.G*el.e.J/el.L)+'.':''}</div>${eq('k<sub>b</sub> = [[a,b,âˆ’a,b], [b,c,âˆ’b,d], [âˆ’a,âˆ’b,a,âˆ’b], [b,d,âˆ’b,c]]')}${model.dimension===3?'<p>Bending-y acts on [wáµ¢, Î¸yáµ¢, wâ±¼, Î¸yâ±¼], with EIáµ§ and b = âˆ’6EIáµ§/LÂ² because Î¸y = âˆ’dw/dx. Torsion uses twist gradient (Î¸xâ±¼ âˆ’ Î¸xáµ¢)/L and torque GJ times this gradient, giving the axial-style block multiplied by GJ/L.</p>':''}<div class="select-row"><label>Contribution <select id="part"><option value="combined">Combined local stiffness</option>${Object.keys(blocks).map(k=>`<option value="${k}" ${part===k?'selected':''}>${k}</option>`).join('')}</select></label></div>${table(active,local,local,true)}<p>Matrix entries carry different units: force/length, force, or forceÂ·length, according to their translation/rotation row and column. E is Youngâ€™s modulus, A area, I the relevant second moment of area${model.dimension===3?', G shear modulus, and J the torsion constant':''}.</p>`;}
 if(stage===2){html=`<h2>Put every member in the same coordinate system.</h2>${selectEl()}<p>T maps global nodal movements to local member movements. Virtual work gives the transpose transformation for forces, so the element stiffness in global axes is:</p>${eq('u<sub>local</sub> = T u<sub>global</sub><br>f<sub>global</sub> = Táµ€ f<sub>local</sub><br>k<sub>global</sub> = Táµ€ k<sub>local</sub> T')}<p>${model.dimension===2?`c = Î”x/L = ${fmt(el.R[0][0])}; s = Î”y/L = ${fmt(el.R[0][1])}. Each nodal block is [[c,s,0], [âˆ’s,c,0], [0,0,1]].`:'Local x is the normalized endpoint vector. Choose reference global z unless |xÂ·z| â‰¥ 0.9, then global y. Set yâ‚€ = normalize(reference Ã— x), zâ‚€ = x Ã— yâ‚€. Roll rotates yâ‚€ and zâ‚€ about x. R has local unit vectors as rows. T contains four copies of R for the two translation and two rotation triples.'}</p><h3 class="subhead">Rotation matrix R (local axes as rows)</h3>${table(el.R,['local x','local y','local z'],['global x','global y','global z'])}<h3 class="subhead">Transformation T</h3>${table(el.T,local,el.map.map(i=>n[i]))}<h3 class="subhead">Transformed element stiffness Táµ€kT</h3>${table(el.kg,el.map.map(i=>n[i]),el.map.map(i=>n[i]),true)}`;}
 if(stage===3){const opts=n.map((x,i)=>`<option value="${i}">${x}</option>`).join('');const terms=r.elements.map(e=>{const i=e.map.indexOf(matrixRow),j=e.map.indexOf(matrixCol);return i>=0&&j>=0?{e,v:e.kg[i][j],i,j}:null;}).filter(Boolean);html=`<h2>Assemble by shared degrees of freedom.</h2>${selectEl()}<p>For each member, add k<sub>global</sub>[i,j] to K[map(i),map(j)]. Shared nodes collect contributions from every connected member; entries are added, never overwritten.</p>${eq('K = Î£ Aâ‚‘áµ€ kâ‚‘,global Aâ‚‘')}<p>Here Aâ‚‘ is a Boolean extraction matrix: it selects the elementâ€™s global DOFs from the complete displacement vector.</p>${table([el.map.map(i=>i+1)],['Global index'],local)}<div class="select-row"><label>Assembly row <select id="assembly-row">${opts}</select></label><label>Column <select id="assembly-col">${opts}</select></label></div><div class="note">K[${n[matrixRow]}, ${n[matrixCol]}] = ${terms.length?terms.map(t=>`E${t.e.e.id}: ${fmt(t.v)} (local slot ${t.i+1},${t.j+1} of transformed matrix)`).join(' + '):'0 (no common member)'} = <strong>${fmt(r.K[matrixRow][matrixCol])}</strong></div><h3 class="subhead">Selected memberâ€™s contribution in the full global system</h3>${table(r.K.map((row,i)=>row.map((_,j)=>{const a=el.map.indexOf(i),b=el.map.indexOf(j);return a>=0&&b>=0?el.kg[a][b]:0;})),n,n,true)}<h3 class="subhead">Complete global stiffness K</h3>${table(r.K,n,n,true)}`;}
 if(stage===4){html=`<h2>Separate known movements from unknowns.</h2><p>Partition the original equations into free (f) and constrained (c) DOFs. A prescribed displacement can be nonzero, so its stiffness contribution must be subtracted from the free load vector.</p>${eq('[Kff Kfc; Kcf Kcc] [uf; uc] = [Ff; Fc + Rc]<br>Kff uf = Ff âˆ’ Kfc uc')}<p>Free DOFs: ${r.free.map(i=>n[i]).join(', ')||'none'}. Constrained DOFs: ${r.fixed.map(i=>n[i]).join(', ')||'none'}.</p><h3 class="subhead">Original global load vector and prescribed values</h3>${table(n.map((_,i)=>[r.F[i],r.fixed.includes(i)?r.u[i]:NaN]),n,['Applied force/moment','Prescribed movement (â€” = free)'])}<h3 class="subhead">Reduced matrix Kff</h3>${r.free.length?table(r.A,r.free.map(i=>n[i]),r.free.map(i=>n[i])):'<p>All movements are prescribed; no reduced solve is needed.</p>'}<h3 class="subhead">Reduced right-hand side</h3>${table(r.free.map((i,j)=>[r.F[i],r.F[i]-r.rhs[j],r.rhs[j]]),r.free.map(i=>n[i]),['Ff','Kfc uc','Ff âˆ’ Kfc uc'])}`;}
 if(stage===5){html=`<h2>Solve the equations, one elimination at a time.</h2><p>The solver uses diagonal scaling followed by Gaussian elimination with partial pivoting and back substitution. Scaling improves numerical balance between translation and rotation equations without changing the physical solution.</p>${eq('Dáµ¢áµ¢ = âˆšKffáµ¢áµ¢; &nbsp; B = Dâ»Â¹KffDâ»Â¹; &nbsp; b = Dâ»Â¹ rhs<br>By = b; &nbsp; uf = Dâ»Â¹y')}<h3 class="subhead">Diagonal scaling</h3>${table(r.scales.map((x,i)=>[x,r.b[i]]),r.free.map(i=>n[i]),['Dii','scaled b'])}`;
 if(r.free.length){const a=r.B.map(row=>row.slice()),b=r.b.slice();for(let k=0;k<elim;k++){const s=r.steps[k],q=s.pivotRow;if(q!==k){[a[k],a[q]]=[a[q],a[k]];[b[k],b[q]]=[b[q],b[k]];}for(const f of s.factors){for(let j=k;j<a.length;j++)a[f.row][j]-=f.factor*a[k][j];b[f.row]-=f.factor*b[k];}}
 html+=`<div class="select-row"><label>Elimination progress <input id="elim" type="range" min="0" max="${r.steps.length}" value="${elim}"></label><span>${elim} / ${r.steps.length} pivots completed</span></div>${table(a.map((row,i)=>row.concat(b[i])),r.free.map((_,i)=>'Row '+(i+1)),r.free.map(i=>n[i]).concat('RHS'))}`;
 if(elim){const s=r.steps[elim-1];html+=`<div class="note">Pivot ${elim}: ${s.pivotRow!==elim-1?`swap rows ${elim} and ${s.pivotRow+1}; `:''}pivot value ${fmt(s.pivot)}. ${s.factors.length?s.factors.map(f=>`R${f.row+1} â† R${f.row+1} âˆ’ (${fmt(f.factor)}) R${elim}`).join('; '):'No rows require elimination.'} Apply the same operation to the RHS.</div>`;}
 html+=`<h3 class="subhead">Back substitution (last row to first)</h3><p>For each row, yáµ¢ = (gáµ¢ âˆ’ Î£â±¼&gt;áµ¢ Uáµ¢â±¼yâ±¼) / Uáµ¢áµ¢. Then divide by Dáµ¢áµ¢ to recover the physical displacement or rotation.</p>${table(r.back.map(x=>[x.rhs,x.sum,x.pivot,x.y,x.y/r.scales[x.row]]),r.back.map(x=>n[r.free[x.row]]),['gáµ¢','Î£ Uáµ¢â±¼yâ±¼','Uáµ¢áµ¢','yáµ¢','uáµ¢ = yáµ¢/Dáµ¢áµ¢'])}`;
 }else html+='<p>Every DOF is prescribed. Recover reactions directly from Ku âˆ’ F.</p>';}
 if(stage===6){html=`<h2>Recover reactions. Interpret the movement.</h2>${eq('R = K u âˆ’ F<br>uâ‚‘,local = T uâ‚‘,global; &nbsp; fâ‚‘,local = kâ‚‘,local uâ‚‘,local')}<p>Use the original unreduced K and applied-load vector F. Constrained entries of R are support reactions; free entries should be approximately zero. Force and moment signs refer to global axes below.</p>${table(r.u.map((v,i)=>[v,r.F[i],r.reactions[i]]),n,['Translation / rotation','Applied force / moment','Reaction / free residual'])}<div class="note">Largest free-DOF residual: ${fmt(r.residual)} in the corresponding force/moment unit. Relative residual: ${fmt(r.relativeResidual)}. Translations: ${esc(model.lengthUnit)}; rotations: rad; forces: ${esc(model.forceUnit)}; moments: ${esc(model.forceUnit)}Â·${esc(model.lengthUnit)}.</div>${selectEl()}${r.fixed.length?'<div class="note">Example reaction at '+n[r.fixed[0]]+': R = '+r.K[r.fixed[0]].map((v,j)=>v!==0?'('+fmt(v)+')('+fmt(r.u[j])+')':null).filter(Boolean).join(' + ')+' âˆ’ ('+fmt(r.F[r.fixed[0]])+') = '+fmt(r.reactions[r.fixed[0]])+'. Each term is Káµ¢â±¼uâ±¼ from the original equilibrium equation.</div>':''}<h3 class="subhead">Member E${el.e.id} â€” local displacement and end-force recovery</h3>${table(el.localU.map((v,i)=>[v,el.forces[i]]),local,['Local movement','Local end force / moment'])}<p>The green shape uses linear axial interpolation and cubic Hermite bending interpolation, including end rotations. The displayed multiplier exaggerates movement; it does not change results.</p>${JSON.stringify(model)===JSON.stringify(FEM.examples.portal())?'<div class="note">Textbook check (rounded): N2.ux â‰ˆ 0.211 in, N2.uy â‰ˆ 0.00148 in, N2.rz â‰ˆ âˆ’0.00153 rad; N3.ux â‰ˆ 0.209 in, N3.uy â‰ˆ âˆ’0.00148 in, N3.rz â‰ˆ âˆ’0.00149 rad. Small differences reflect rounding of the textbook stiffness coefficients.</div>':''}${JSON.stringify(model)===JSON.stringify(FEM.examples.spatial())?'<div class="note">Analytical check: ux = Fx L/EA; uy = Fy LÂ³/(3EIá¶»); uz = Fz LÂ³/(3EIÊ¸); rx = Mx L/GJ; ry = âˆ’Fz LÂ²/(2EIÊ¸); rz = Fy LÂ²/(2EIá¶»). This example exercises axial, two bending, and torsional responses.</div>':''}`;}
 $('lesson').innerHTML=html;
 if($('element-select'))$('element-select').onchange=e=>{selected=+e.target.value;renderLesson();draw();};if($('part'))$('part').onchange=e=>{part=e.target.value;renderLesson();};
 if($('assembly-row')){ $('assembly-row').value=matrixRow;$('assembly-col').value=matrixCol;$('assembly-row').onchange=e=>{matrixRow=+e.target.value;renderLesson();};$('assembly-col').onchange=e=>{matrixCol=+e.target.value;renderLesson();};}
 if($('elim'))$('elim').oninput=e=>{elim=+e.target.value;renderLesson();};
}
function draw(){const dim=model.dimension,az=+$('azimuth').value*Math.PI/180,ev=+$('elevation').value*Math.PI/180,scale=Math.max(0,+$('scale').value||0),show=result&&$('show-deformed').checked;
 const raw=q=>dim===2?[q[0],-q[1]]:[q[0]*Math.cos(az)-q[1]*Math.sin(az),-(q[0]*Math.sin(az)+q[1]*Math.cos(az))*Math.sin(ev)-q[2]*Math.cos(ev)];
 const coords=n=>[n.x,n.y,dim===3?n.z:0],all=model.nodes.map(n=>raw(coords(n))).filter(q=>q.every(Number.isFinite));
 if(show)for(const el of result.elements)for(let i=0;i<=20;i++){const t=i/20,disp=FEM.curve(el,dim,t),a=coords(el.a),b=coords(el.b);all.push(raw(a.map((v,j)=>v+(b[j]-v)*t+scale*disp[j])));}
 if(!all.length){$('drawing').innerHTML='';return;}const xs=all.map(q=>q[0]),ys=all.map(q=>q[1]),xmin=Math.min(...xs),xmax=Math.max(...xs),ymin=Math.min(...ys),ymax=Math.max(...ys),s=Math.min(570/Math.max(xmax-xmin,1e-12),220/Math.max(ymax-ymin,1e-12)),center=[(xmin+xmax)/2,(ymin+ymax)/2],proj=q=>{const v=raw(q);return [400+(v[0]-center[0])*s,170+(v[1]-center[1])*s];};
 let svg='<svg viewBox="0 0 800 360" role="img" aria-label="Structural model with nodes, members, loads, supports and deformed shape"><defs><marker id="arrow" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" refX="6" refY="3" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L6,3 L0,6" fill="#ba663d"/></marker><marker id="axis" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" refX="5" refY="3" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L5,3 L0,6" fill="#658981"/></marker></defs>';
 for(let i=0;i<model.elements.length;i++){const el=model.elements[i],a=model.nodes.find(n=>n.id===el.a),b=model.nodes.find(n=>n.id===el.b);if(!a||!b)continue;const pa=proj(coords(a)),pb=proj(coords(b)),mx=(pa[0]+pb[0])/2,my=(pa[1]+pb[1])/2;svg+=`<line class="member-hit" data-member="${i}" x1="${pa[0]}" y1="${pa[1]}" x2="${pb[0]}" y2="${pb[1]}" stroke="transparent" stroke-width="22"><title>Inspect member ${el.id}</title></line><line pointer-events="none" x1="${pa[0]}" y1="${pa[1]}" x2="${pb[0]}" y2="${pb[1]}" stroke="${i===selected?'#183f42':'#506467'}" stroke-width="${i===selected?4:3}"/><rect x="${mx-12}" y="${my-22}" width="26" height="19" rx="5" fill="#e7eee6"/><text x="${mx+1}" y="${my-9}" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="#345951">E${el.id}</text>`;}
 if(show)for(const el of result.elements){const a=coords(el.a),b=coords(el.b),points=[];for(let i=0;i<=30;i++){const t=i/30,u=FEM.curve(el,dim,t);points.push(proj(a.map((v,j)=>v+(b[j]-v)*t+scale*u[j])).join(','));}svg+=`<polyline points="${points.join(' ')}" fill="none" stroke="#087f77" stroke-width="2.5" pointer-events="none"/>`;}
 for(const nd of model.nodes){const q=proj(coords(nd)),[x,y]=q,bc=nd.prescribed.map((v,i)=>v!==null?FEM.labels(dim)[i]+'='+v:null).filter(Boolean);if(bc.length){const fixed=bc.length===p();svg+=fixed?`<path d="M${x-11},${y+8} h22 m-22,4 h22 m-20,0 l-5,6 m12,-6 l-5,6 m12,-6 l-5,6" stroke="#72867a" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none"><title>${esc(bc.join(', '))}</title></path>`:`<path d="M${x},${y+3} l-10,15 h20 Z" fill="#e5eddf" stroke="#72867a"><title>${esc(bc.join(', '))}</title></path>`;}
 svg+=`<circle cx="${x}" cy="${y}" r="5" fill="white" stroke="#183f42" stroke-width="2"><title>N${nd.id}: (${coords(nd).map(fmt).join(', ')}); DOFs ${FEM.labels(dim).join(', ')}</title></circle><text x="${x+10}" y="${y-10}" font-size="12" fill="#183f42">N${nd.id}</text>`;
 const tr=dim===2?2:3;for(let j=0;j<tr;j++)if(nd.loads[j]){const axis=[0,0,0];axis[j]=1;const v=raw(axis),len=Math.hypot(...v);const dx=len>1e-8?v[0]/len*45*Math.sign(nd.loads[j]):0,dy=len>1e-8?v[1]/len*45*Math.sign(nd.loads[j]):0;svg+=`<line x1="${x-dx}" y1="${y-dy}" x2="${x}" y2="${y}" stroke="#ba663d" stroke-width="1.8" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/><text x="${x-dx+5}" y="${y-dy-8-12*j}" font-size="10" fill="#a44f2b">F${'xyz'[j]}=${fmt(nd.loads[j])}</text>`;}
 for(let j=tr;j<p();j++)if(nd.loads[j])svg+=`<text x="${x+12}" y="${y+24+13*(j-tr)}" fill="#a44f2b" font-size="10">â†¶ M${FEM.labels(dim)[j].slice(1)}=${fmt(nd.loads[j])}</text>`;
 }
 // Global orientation triad in the view corner.
 const axes=dim===2?['x','y']:['x','y','z'];for(let j=0;j<axes.length;j++){const v=[0,0,0];v[j]=1;const a=raw(v);svg+=`<line x1="55" y1="300" x2="${55+a[0]*32}" y2="${300+a[1]*32}" stroke="#658981" marker-end="url(#axis)"/><text x="${55+a[0]*42}" y="${304+a[1]*42}" font-size="11" fill="#658981">${axes[j]}</text>`;}
 if(result&&result.elements[selected]){const e=result.elements[selected],a=coords(e.a),b=coords(e.b),mid=a.map((v,j)=>(v+b[j])/2),o=proj(mid);for(let j=0;j<(dim===2?2:3);j++){const v=raw(e.R[j]),end=[o[0]+v[0]*28,o[1]+v[1]*28];svg+=`<line pointer-events="none" x1="${o[0]}" y1="${o[1]}" x2="${end[0]}" y2="${end[1]}" stroke="#658981" stroke-dasharray="3 2" marker-end="url(#axis)"/><text x="${end[0]+3}" y="${end[1]+3}" fill="#658981" font-size="9">${'xyz'[j]}â€²</text>`;}}
 svg+=`<text x="775" y="338" text-anchor="end" font-size="10" fill="#74877c">${show?'DEFORMATION Ã— '+fmt(scale):'UNDEFORMED'} Â· ${esc(model.lengthUnit)} / ${esc(model.forceUnit)}</text></svg>`;$('drawing').innerHTML=svg;
}
$('drawing').onclick=e=>{const t=e.target.closest('[data-member]');if(t){selected=+t.dataset.member;stage=1;renderLesson();draw();}};
$('solve').onclick=solve;$('example').onchange=e=>{model=FEM.examples[e.target.value]();selected=0;stage=0;part='combined';$('scale').value=model.dimension===2?100:40;renderEditor();solve();};
$('stages').onclick=e=>{if(e.target.dataset.stage!==undefined){stage=+e.target.dataset.stage;renderLesson();}};$('prev').onclick=()=>{stage=Math.max(0,stage-1);renderLesson();};$('next').onclick=()=>{stage=Math.min(stages.length-1,stage+1);renderLesson();};
for(const id of ['show-deformed','scale','azimuth','elevation'])$(id).oninput=draw;
for(const id of ['length-unit','force-unit'])$(id).onchange=e=>{model[id==='length-unit'?'lengthUnit':'forceUnit']=e.target.value;renderLesson();draw();if(result)solve();};
document.querySelectorAll('[data-edit]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{edit=b.dataset.edit;renderEditor();});
function download(name,text,type='application/json'){const blob=new Blob([text],{type}),url=URL.createObjectURL(blob),a=document.createElement('a');a.href=url;a.download=name;a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(url),1000);}
$('export').onclick=()=>download('framelab-model.json',JSON.stringify(model,null,2));
$('import').onchange=async e=>{try{const candidate=JSON.parse(await e.target.files[0].text());FEM.solve(candidate);model={...candidate,name:String(candidate.name||'Imported model'),lengthUnit:String(candidate.lengthUnit||'m'),forceUnit:String(candidate.forceUnit||'N')};selected=0;stage=0;renderEditor();solve();}catch(err){$('error').textContent='Could not open model: '+err.message;}e.target.value='';};
const guide=`<h2>Your guide to FrameLab</h2><p>Build a frame, then follow the same sequence you would use in a manual stiffness-method calculation.</p><ol><li><strong>Choose an example.</strong> The portal frame reproduces the supplied textbook example. The combined-load 3D cantilever has independent analytical checks; the bent frame demonstrates arbitrary spatial orientation.</li><li><strong>Edit nodes.</strong> Set coordinates in a consistent unit system. Add or remove nodes with the buttons. Deleting a node also deletes attached members.</li><li><strong>Set supports.</strong> â€œFixedâ€ restrains every DOF. â€œPinnedâ€ restrains translations and allows rotations. â€œFreeâ€ releases every DOF. Check an individual DOF and enter a value for prescribed displacement or rotation. Use these individual controls for rollers or partial restraints.</li><li><strong>Edit members.</strong> Choose the start/end nodes and positive section/material values. E and G have force/lengthÂ² units, A lengthÂ², I and J lengthâ´. In 3D, roll is degrees; all solved or prescribed rotations are radians.</li><li><strong>Apply loads.</strong> Enter nodal forces and moments along global axes. Moments use force Ã— length units. Positive rotations follow the right-hand rule.</li><li><strong>Solve & explore.</strong> Visit all seven stages. Inspect individual members, select axial/bending/torsional contributions, examine global assembly entries, and advance the elimination slider.</li><li><strong>Inspect the result.</strong> Green curves use the selected deformation multiplier. Orbit/elevation controls rotate the 3D projection. The results stage lists translations, rotations, support reactions, and member end forces.</li><li><strong>Save your work.</strong> Save model downloads a JSON file. Open model restores a valid saved model. The full downloadable submission runs by opening dist/index.html, without installation or internet.</li></ol><p><strong>Unit examples:</strong> use N, m, E = 210Ã—10â¹ N/mÂ² and moments in NÂ·m; or lb, in, E = 30Ã—10â¶ lb/inÂ² and moments in lbÂ·in. Unit labels do not convert numbers.</p><p><strong>Validation:</strong> zero-length members, invalid properties, missing endpoints, and singular systems produce clear errors. There is no fixed node/member limit; dense matrix memory and computation determine practical size.</p><p><strong>Scope:</strong> small-displacement, linear elastic Eulerâ€“Bernoulli prismatic frames, rigid member connections, nodal loading. Internal hinges, distributed member loads, tapered sections, shear deformation, and nonlinear buckling are not implemented. The supplied second test PDF contains multiple special beam exercises without identifying a target; these are not claimed as supported validation cases.</p><p><strong>3D section orientation:</strong> x points from the start to end node. Reference is global z unless nearly parallel, then global y. yâ‚€ = normalize(reference Ã— x), zâ‚€ = x Ã— yâ‚€. Positive roll sends yâ‚€ toward zâ‚€. Iy and Iz refer to the resulting local axes.</p><p><strong>Test case 1:</strong> geometry is converted to inches: columns and beam are 120 in. E = 30Ã—10â¶ psi, A = 10 inÂ²; columns Iz = 200 inâ´, beam Iz = 100 inâ´. Fx at node 2 is 10,000 lb; Mz at node 3 is 5,000 lbÂ·in. Compare rounded displacements in the Results stage.</p>`;
function modal(content){$('modal-body').innerHTML=content;$('modal').showModal();}$('guide').onclick=()=>modal(guide);$('disclosure').onclick=()=>modal('<h2>AI usage disclosure</h2><p>OpenAI Codex assisted with interpreting the assignment, implementing the FEM engine and interface, preparing documentation, and constructing automated validation checks. The finished tool uses explicitly programmed equations, matrix assembly, Gaussian elimination, and fixed explanatory templates. It makes no AI, chatbot, LLM, or other external service calls during operation.</p>');$('close-modal').onclick=()=>$('modal').close();
renderEditor();solve();
</script></body></html>

